course: dictionary
lesson: 347
title: Anonymous: a name nobody knows
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anonymous means made, given or done by someone whose name is not known or not told. The word is made of parts: an- means "without" and -onym means "name", so anonymous means "without a name". Use the words around it to check.
explain: «An anonymous forum post is not news, and children's lives should never be dragged into gossip.» The clue is that the post has no name on it. Swap in "a post with no name" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Anonymous can also describe a thing. «An anonymous grey building» is plain and dull, with nothing special about it. Ask yourself: is the word about a person's name, or about something ordinary? The sentence tells you which.
fact: Anonymous means not named, or with a name that nobody knows or has told.
fact: «Anonymous» can describe a person, a gift, a letter, or a plain building.
fact: «Remain anonymous» means to stay without your name being known.
fact: In poetry books, «Anon.» means the poet's name is unknown.
fact: Being anonymous online does not make hurtful words hurt less; real people read them.
exercise: «The gift to the charity came from an anonymous donor.» What does anonymous mean here? | A donor who is very tall | A donor who gives money every day | *A donor whose name is not told | A donor who lives in a castle
exercise: Find the word that means not known by name: «The letter was anonymous, so nobody knew who had written it.» | *anonymous | written | letter | nobody
exercise: «An anonymous grey building stood at the end of the street.» What does anonymous suggest here? | Loud and busy with people | *Plain and dull, with nothing special about it | Very old and full of ghosts | Bright, colourful and famous
test: «Anonymous reporting means telling without giving your name.» What does this sentence mean? | Giving your name to every person | *Telling something without giving your name | Writing a long report about names | Reporting the news on television
test: «Being anonymous online doesn't make hurtful words hurt less.» What is the message? | Hurtful words hurt less when no name is shown | *Real people read hurtful words, even when the writer is anonymous | Anonymous online users cannot be seen | Nobody reads anything posted without a name
exam: Priya says anonymous means famous. Which is correct? | Anonymous means very old | Anonymous means a loud noise | Anonymous means famous and well known | *Anonymous means someone's name is not known or not told
